{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793168324871948146,"compiled_state":{"alias":"orchestral-curious-foxterrier","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"d4d52a2becceb5a3e0ff42deac0fb9e61b78f13ad479f6b66b1394f73b2b027a","event_uuid":"8c6237e4-a87c-44cb-a112-d81291ed4884","position":{"commit_sha":"65037cef93f24759b6ba480d932958b16b04f412","position":"1793146438994930691-8c6237e4-a87c-44cb-a112-d81291ed4884"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e08687e1387c09cf484cd4efd773ce7bd28d573d2167f736c2b22cf256042560","event_uuid":"4f3c1e4d-6a8e-49d7-8e64-53915c507b30","position":{"commit_sha":"63555558e5c2ef31d3d90235ad659a69ef8a8bd3","position":"1793146446839130240-4f3c1e4d-6a8e-49d7-8e64-53915c507b30"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793146438994930691,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4f3c1e4d-6a8e-49d7-8e64-53915c507b30","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1064-8c4a-f399-41de"}],"description":"## Problem\nThe expected dedicated-mount set is hardcoded per volume in three places: infra/terraform/user_data.sh, infra/scripts/check-mounts.sh (hardcoded /var/gerrit /var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch), and infra/scripts/observability.sh (DATA_MOUNT, GATE_SCRATCH_MOUNT). A third volume added later gets no metric and no alarm until someone writes it into each place by hand.\n\nSplit from the closed bug 1064-8c4a-f399-41de (its residual AC4); the refusal-inert part of that bug was fixed by be40fd250fd.\n\n## Approach\nMake the mount set data (one list, single-sourced from terraform) and have the periodic probe iterate it, so present and future volumes share one alarm. tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py already pins agreement between consumers and is the place to extend.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The expected mount set is declared once; check-mounts.sh and observability.sh read it rather than hardcoding paths.\n- [ ] A test adds a hypothetical third mount and shows the probe covers it without editing the scripts.\n- [ ] make verify exits 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c400-fec0-a7bf-4755","ticket_type":"task","title":"Expected gate-scratch mount set is written by hand in three places, so a new volume gets no metric or alarm","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8c6237e4-a87c-44cb-a112-d81291ed4884","4f3c1e4d-6a8e-49d7-8e64-53915c507b30"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793168324871948146,"uuid":"c615bf33-ea1c-42a0-b587-7bc37a1fdd6c"}